#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""phone — drive an Android device as a fabric surface.

The device analog of anu's `pane` and `nv`: one verb layer over the two
mechanisms an unrooted Android phone actually offers.

  termux-api   the device as a peripheral — speak, listen, notifications,
               camera, torch, location, clipboard, SMS.
  adb (self)   the device as a screen — see it (screencap), read it as text
               (uiautomator), touch it (input), launch it (am start).
               adb is connected from the phone TO ITSELF over wireless
               debugging, so no PC is tethered and nothing leaves the device.

Everything an agent needs is a verb here, so the brain never has to know
whether a capability comes from termux-api or adb. Any agent on the fabric —
local (ember) or remote (fable on the mini, crucible on the 88-core box) —
drives the phone by calling these verbs.

Stdlib only. Runs on the phone, in Termux.

The parsing verbs (`ui`, `find`, `notifs`) accept `--from FILE` so the logic
that an LLM depends on is testable off-device.
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
